body:
@hansl  how would you load it with a string? 

when I try to put something like `{ path: 'lazy', loadChildren: './features/lazy#LazyModule' }` that does't seem to work at all with webpack.

Both of the ones below work fine in JIT, but not AOT.

```
export function loadLazy() {
  return require('es6-promise!./features/lazy')('LazyModule');
}

//or

export function loadLazy() {
  return System.import('./features/lazy').then((r: any) => r.LazyModule);
}
```

Is there any current solution for us that are using Webpack 2, but not CLI?
